---
// INTERNAL TOOL — not linked from anywhere, excluded from sitemap, noindex.
// WhatsApp lead-handling scripts for the ₹5,000 anchored Shopify store offer.
const updated = "11 August 2026";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex" />
    <meta name="googlebot" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer" />
    <title>WhatsApp Lead Scripts — Internal</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        --cream: #f5efe6;
        --charcoal: #2b2b2b;
        --terracotta: #c96f4a;
        --muted: #7d746a;
        --line: #e3d9cc;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--cream);
        color: var(--charcoal);
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Inter, Roboto, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }
      .wrap { max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 20px 96px; }
      header.page { border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 20px; margin-bottom: 36px; }
      h1 { font-size: 30px; margin: 0 0 6px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin: 0; }
      h2 {
        font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.09em;
        color: var(--terracotta); margin: 44px 0 14px; font-weight: 700;
      }
      h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 22px 0 8px; }
      p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
      .note {
        font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); background: #fff;
        border-left: 3px solid var(--terracotta); padding: 12px 14px;
        border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin: 0 0 18px;
      }
      .msg {
        position: relative; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 12px; margin: 0 0 16px; overflow: hidden;
      }
      .msg pre {
        margin: 0; padding: 18px 18px 18px; white-space: pre-wrap; word-wrap: break-word;
        font-family: inherit; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65;
      }
      .copy {
        position: absolute; top: 10px; right: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line);
        background: var(--cream); color: var(--charcoal); font: inherit; font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 600; padding: 5px 12px; border-radius: 999px; cursor: pointer;
        transition: background .15s, color .15s, border-color .15s;
      }
      .copy:hover { background: var(--terracotta); color: #fff; border-color: var(--terracotta); }
      .copy.done { background: #1f7a4d; color: #fff; border-color: #1f7a4d; }
      ol.order { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 18px 18px 38px; }
      ol.order li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
      ul.rules li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
      hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 40px 0; }
      .tag {
        display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em;
        text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--terracotta); color: #fff;
        padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 999px; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 8px;
      }
      footer.page { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="page">
        <h1>WhatsApp Lead Scripts<span class="tag">Internal</span></h1>
        <p class="sub">India · ₹5,000 anchored offer · updated {updated}</p>
      </header>

      <p class="note">
        Use "I" throughout, never a mix of I/we. Reply within 15 minutes — speed beats wording.
        A perfect message four hours late loses to a decent one in ten minutes.
      </p>

      <h2>Message order at a glance</h2>
      <ol class="order">
        <li>Anchor story (₹45,000 → ₹5,000, with the reason)</li>
        <li>Proof + "what do you sell?"</li>
        <li><em>They reply</em></li>
        <li>Shopify fee disclosure</li>
        <li>Scoping questions + how I work</li>
        <li><em>They send products</em></li>
        <li>Free mockup</li>
        <li>Close with 50/50 payment</li>
      </ol>

      <hr />

      <h2>1 · Opening</h2>
      <p class="note">Send as two separate messages. Two short bubbles read as a person; one long block reads as a broadcast.</p>

      <h3>Message A — the story</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Hi! Mukesh here from Capaxe Labs 👋

My usual rate to build a Shopify store is ₹45,000.

I'm doing the next 50 stores at ₹5,000 to reach Shopify Partner status — after that it goes back to normal pricing.</pre>
      </div>

      <h3>Message B — proof + the one ask <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px">(attach 2 store screenshots)</span></h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Here's the kind of store I build ⬆️

Design, all pages, mobile-ready, handed over in 48 hours.

What do you sell? Send me your Instagram or a few product photos and I'll put together a free mockup for you — no commitment.</pre>
      </div>

      <hr />

      <h2>2 · Shopify fee — say it before they find it</h2>
      <p class="note">Send as soon as they reply. Must happen before the store-transfer step, or a paid project turns into a refund request. Check Shopify's current India promo so the number is accurate.</p>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>One thing so there are no surprises later:

The ₹5,000 is my fee — design, pages, setup, handover.

Shopify charges their own monthly plan directly (they usually run a heavily discounted first few months for new stores). I'll show you exactly what it costs before you commit to anything.</pre>
      </div>

      <hr />

      <h2>3 · Scoping — only after they've said what they sell</h2>
      <p class="note">Never send this as message 1 or 2. A stranger who tapped an ad 90 seconds ago will not fill a form. After they engage, it reads as professional scoping instead of a gate.</p>

      <h3>Bubble 1 — the questions</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Great, thanks! A few quick questions so I can scope this properly — these decide how big or small the build is:

1. How many products, roughly?
2. Any design or reference website you like?
3. Are you selling online anywhere already?
4. Do you have a domain name yet?

Rough answers are completely fine.</pre>
      </div>

      <h3>Bubble 2 — how I work</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Here's how I work:

1. You share the above, I scope it and confirm
2. I build the store and set up the structure
3. I transfer it to your Shopify account
4. I implement your design and specific requirements
5. Once you're live, a short review from you would mean a lot 🙏

Share as much detail as you can — the more I know, the better the fit.</pre>
      </div>

      <hr />

      <h2>4 · After they send products</h2>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Got it — thanks 🙏

Give me a few hours and I'll send you a mockup of your homepage with your actual products in it.</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Then actually send the mockup. Their own products in a real design creates reciprocity and makes the store real in their head. Almost nobody at this price does it — it is the strongest conversion tool in the sequence.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>5 · The close</h2>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Here's your store mockup ⬆️

If you like it, I can have the full thing live in 48 hours. ₹5,000, half now and half on handover.

Want me to start?</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Splitting payment halves the perceived risk of buying from a stranger online.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>6 · Follow-ups for ghosts</h2>
      <p class="note">Two, then stop. Chasing further wastes your time and annoys people.</p>

      <h3>After ~24 hours</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Hey — still keen on the store? Happy to do that free mockup whenever you're ready, just send a few product photos 🙂</pre>
      </div>

      <h3>After ~72 hours</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Closing out this week's slots — I take a limited number at the ₹5,000 rate. Want me to hold one for you?</pre>
      </div>

      <hr />

      <h2>7 · Objection handling</h2>

      <h3>"Too expensive"</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Fair — for reference, agencies quote ₹40,000-₹1,00,000 for the same thing, and my own regular rate is ₹45,000. The ₹5,000 exists only because I need 50 stores for Partner status. It won't be available later.</pre>
      </div>

      <h3>"Can you do it cheaper?"</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Not at ₹5,000, sorry — it's already ~90% off my normal rate. What I can do is start with a simpler version and add pages later once you're selling.</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Never discount below ₹5,000. ₹500 was already tested and attracted people who don't buy.</p>

      <h3>"Why so cheap? What's the catch?"</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>No catch. Shopify gives agency benefits once you've built a certain number of stores. I need 50. You get a ₹45,000 store for ₹5,000, I get closer to Partner status. That's the whole deal.</pre>
      </div>

      <h3>"I'll think about it"</h3>
      <div class="msg">
        <button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <pre>Of course. Want me to do the free mockup in the meantime? Costs you nothing and you'll know exactly what you'd be getting.</pre>
      </div>

      <h3>"Can I see your past work?"</h3>
      <p>Send 2-3 screenshots or live links immediately. If you don't have any yet, build one demo store this week — it pays for itself on the first lead.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Rules</h2>
      <ul class="rules">
        <li><strong>Reply within 15 minutes.</strong> Speed beats wording.</li>
        <li><strong>Never ask two questions in one message</strong> — except section 3, which is deliberate and comes only after engagement.</li>
        <li><strong>Never lead with a question.</strong> Lead with the anchor and the proof.</li>
        <li><strong>Say the Shopify fee before they ask</strong>, and always before the transfer step.</li>
        <li><strong>Always offer the free mockup.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Voice notes work well in India</strong> once a lead is engaged.</li>
        <li><strong>Track per lead:</strong> which ad they came from, whether they replied to message 2, whether they paid.</li>
      </ul>

      <footer class="page">
        Internal page — noindex, excluded from sitemap, not linked from anywhere on the site.
      </footer>
    </div>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll(".copy").forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
          const pre = btn.parentElement.querySelector("pre");
          if (!pre) return;
          try {
            await navigator.clipboard.writeText(pre.textContent.trim());
          } catch (e) {
            const r = document.createRange();
            r.selectNodeContents(pre);
            const s = window.getSelection();
            s.removeAllRanges();
            s.addRange(r);
            document.execCommand("copy");
            s.removeAllRanges();
          }
          const original = btn.textContent;
          btn.textContent = "Copied";
          btn.classList.add("done");
          setTimeout(() => {
            btn.textContent = original;
            btn.classList.remove("done");
          }, 1500);
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
